<bioghist encodinganalog="545$a">
<head>Biographical Information
</head>
<p>Ezra Basil Hensley was born 14 December 1910 in Albemarle County, Virginia, to William Thomas Hensley (1878-1967) and Maggie Lee Haney Hensley (1873-1924).  Hensley became an operating engineer in construction.  During World War II, he was a technician level 5 in the United States Army.  After the war, he returned to work as an operating engineer, settling in Alexandria, Virginia.  Hensley died 8 Marcy 1986 in Alexandria.  He married Grace Mae Wood on 29 June 1946.  Grace Wood was born 8 January 1924 in Albemarle County to Ray Otto Wood (1892-1961) and Mattie Allen Wood (1890-1980).  Grace Hensley died 8 June 2002 in Spotsylvania County, Virginia.  Ezra Hensley and Grace Wood Hensley are buried in the National Cemetery at Quantico, Virginia.  They had two daughters, Grace Elaine Hensley and Melva Allen Hensley.
</p>
</bioghist>
<scopecontent encodinganalog="520$a">
<head>Scope and Content
</head>
<p>Papers, 1930-1986, of the Hensley family of Alexandria, Virginia, consisting of papers, 1938-1986, of Ezra Basil Hensley (1910-1986) concerning his service in the United States army and his career as an operating engineer; grade cards, 1930-1941, of Grace Wood (Hensley) (1924-2002) and book on child-rearing; grade cards and papers, 1958-1979, for Grace Elaine Hensley and Melva Allen Hensley attending Fairfax County, Virginia, public schools and Northern Virginia Community College.
</p>
</scopecontent>
